 {
  "id": "corpus:wwr-superplane-product-engineer-1",
  "title": "Product Engineer",
  "text": "Headquarters:\nUSA\n\nURL:\n\nhttps://superplane.com\n\nWe are hiring a product engineer to join SuperPlane and own meaningful projects end to end.\n\nThis is a remote role. We currently work across GMT+2 to GMT-3 and welcome candidates in that range.\n\nAt SuperPlane, we don't split engineering into frontend and backend. Everyone is a well-rounded builder who moves across the stack, makes product and technical calls, asks for help when needed, and delivers features from start to finish. You might spend one day building an API endpoint or workflow engine improvement, and the next day polishing a React surface that users touch every day.\n\nWe're looking for someone at a mid-level to senior level: you've shipped real products, you can work independently, and you're ready to grow fast in a high-trust, high-pace environment. You don't need to have done everything before, but you need to learn quickly and take ownership of what you build.\n\n\n\nWhat We Are Looking For\n\nYou are genuinely full-stack.\n\nYour workflow is AI-driven and you know how to stay fast without getting sloppy.\n\nYou have strong backend experience in a systems-oriented language. While we use Go, we don't expect you to be an expert already, just to ramp up fast.\n\nYou have solid systems judgment. APIs, data models, reliability, and trade-offs matter to you.\n\nYou're comfortable with TypeScript and React -- the modern frontend stack.\n\nYou are comfortable with cloud-native tooling and modern software delivery.\n\nYou want ownership, not a narrow lane.\n\nYou want an early-stage company where the pace is high, the standards are high, and the upside is big.\n\n\n\nHow To Apply\n\nWe care more about proof of work than polished applications, and we want to see how you show up in open source.\n\nBefore you apply, submit at least one pull request to superplanehq/superplane. It can be small and it does not need to be merged.\n\nWhen you apply, send your GitHub username and a link to your pull request. We verify both, and applications missing either field will not move forward.\n\n\n\nWhy You'll Love Working at SuperPlane\n\nBuild a frontier product used by engineers across the globe.\n\nMeaningful equity and real ownership.\n\nSmall team, fast feedback loops.\n\nRemote role that lets you focus and create.\n\nTo apply:\n\nhttps://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/superplane-product-engineer-1",
  "requires": false,
  "note": "stored advert: 'While we use Go, we don't expect you to be an expert already'",
